<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">How we separate evidence</p>
  <h2>Use the evidence that matches the question</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4">
    <article><h3>Established physiology</h3><p>Explains processes such as fluid balance and sodium-glucose transport.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Formulation rationale</h3><p>Explains why ingredients and concentrations are selected.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Product research</h3><p>Tests the finished formulation under defined conditions.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Application evidence</h3><p>Tests whether findings translate to a particular population or setting.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Research collaboration</p>
    <h2>Roles and affiliations should be clear</h2>
    <p>Dr. Spencer Proctor is Professor and Department Chair in Agricultural, Food and Nutritional Science at the University of Alberta, Director of the Metabolic and Cardiovascular Diseases Laboratory and Chief Scientific Officer of Best Hydrate. He is also a co-author of the published Frontiers hydration review.</p>
    <p>His university role provides relevant expertise; it does not mean the University of Alberta endorses Best Hydrate or every product claim.</p>
  </article>
